      "main": "Why Does the UK Keep Inventing Music.",
      "sub": "50 years. 10 genres. One thread."
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "Population: 66 million.",
        "Land: smaller than Japan.",
        "In 50 years —",
        "more than ten new genres."
      ],
      "sub": "Why the UK."
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "1950s. Jamaican immigrants arrived in London.",
        "They were not allowed in clubs.",
        "So they brought speakers into the streets.",
        "That was the sound system."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "1980s. Thatcher closed the factories.",
        "Young people had nowhere to go.",
        "No money.",
        "So they made music."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "quote",
      "quote": [
        "Every time the mainstream shut a door,",
        "the underground opened a floor."
      ],
      "note": "Excluded people build their own spaces. Every time."
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "Dub. Punk. Acid House. Jungle.",
        "Drum and Bass. UK Garage. Dubstep. Grime.",
        "These are not separate genres.",
        "This is one line."
      ],
      "bg_anchor_y": 0.7
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "UK music carries the smell of wounds.",
        "Poverty was the fuel.",
        "Exclusion was the spark.",
        "The underground is the record."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "cta",
      "text": [
        "The line has not ended.",
        "It is still being written."
      ],
      "strobe": ["Boredom, poverty, exclusion.", "That is the formula."],
